WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.160
In the fly embryo, the cells that will make the nervous system sit in small groups.

2
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.780
The cells start out equal, and every cell can become a neural precursor.

3
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.300
Yet usually only one does.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.820
Something must break the tie.

5
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.700
First the group becomes able, and then the cells signal to each other until one

6
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.700
wins.

7
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:25.333
Take two neighbours in the cluster.

8
00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:30.213
pro -neural genes and code transcription factors that make both cells able to become

9
00:00:30.213 --> 00:00:34.573
neural. Think of it as a casting call, where everyone gets to audition.

10
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:39.653
Pro -neural proteins raise their own expression, and in the textbook model they also

11
00:00:39.653 --> 00:00:42.893
raise Delta. Delta is a protein in the cell membrane.

12
00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:47.737
Delta on one cell binds Notch on the cell it touches, and pulls.

13
00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:50.677
Two cuts then free the inner part of Notch.

14
00:00:51.297 --> 00:00:52.857
That part enters the nucleus.

15
00:00:53.497 --> 00:00:58.417
There, with a protein called CSL, it turns on the Enhancer of split genes.

16
00:00:59.037 --> 00:01:02.497
These genes encode repressors that switch proneural genes off.

17
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:09.340
Follow the loop. More Delta on cell A means more Notch activity in cell B. Cell B

18
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.340
makes more repressor, so it has less proneural activity and less Delta.

19
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.880
Then cell A gets less Notch activity, and its proneural activity rises.

20
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.920
The loop has closed, and cell A has pulled ahead.

21
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:26.233
Each cell inhibits its neighbour, so two inhibitions in a row make positive

22
00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:31.013
feedback. With strong enough feedback, a balanced pair sits like a pencil on its

23
00:01:31.013 --> 00:01:36.493
point. But noise gives one cell slightly more Delta, and the loop magnifies that

24
00:01:36.493 --> 00:01:38.673
until one cell becomes the neural precursor.

25
00:01:39.413 --> 00:01:43.613
Either outcome is stable, and in this ideal pair the winner is a matter of chance.

26
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:46.463
Now take Notch away from the embryo.

27
00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:50.003
Without the receptor, no cell can be told, not you.

28
00:01:50.663 --> 00:01:54.443
Both cells keep their proneural genes on, and both become neural.

29
00:01:54.943 --> 00:01:58.943
In the whole embryo, that means far too many neuroblasts and too little skin.

30
00:01:59.543 --> 00:02:04.523
In fly mosaics, what decides a cell's fate is how its signaling compares with its

31
00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:04.763
neighbours.
